Webinar: ML Model and Dual Core Debugging on Alif Ensemble E7&nbsp;

This is your final reminder to join our upcoming live webinar.&nbsp;

&#128198; Happening: Aug 12, 2025
&#9200; Time: 9 a.m. PDT | 4 p.m. BST | 5 p.m. CET&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Get ready to unlock powerful multicore debugging and ML development on the Alif Ensemble E7 with Keil Studio. Learn how to streamline AI workflows across Arm Cortex-M55 and Arm Ethos-U55 cores using Jupyter notebooks and Visual Studio Code.&nbsp;

Secure Your Spot https://goto.arm.com/NDc5LVpZVy05MDcAAAGcOIRNql4U9yG0XdcjXB9-geHwFbrbQizhqTfMsR-uu-pOmbxcGhXiXcCIzVuXFeUIpe6A9Tk=
In this session, you get hands-on guidance with:
  &nbsp;
   How to set up and manage dual-core projects for the Alif Ensemble E7. How to debug Cortex-M55 and Ethos-U55 cores in a synchronized workflow. How to analyze runtime behavior and inspect memory and registers across multiple cores. How to integrate and validate ML models on embedded targets. How to retrain ML models efficiently using Jupyter notebooks in VS Code&nbsp;





